# Maestro

Flows live in `.maestro/` and run against the **development** flavor only.

## Rebuild before run (required)

Maestro exercises the **installed** app on the device/emulator, not hot-reload or workspace source. If **any** Dart change landed since the last install (UI, semantics IDs, routing, flavor config), **rebuild and reinstall the development flavor before** `maestro test`, Maestro MCP `run`, or asking the human to verify flows:

```bash
cd sprout_app
flutter build apk --debug --flavor development -t lib/main_development.dart
flutter install --debug --flavor development
```

For day-to-day iteration, `flutter run --flavor development -t lib/main_development.dart` on the target device is enough — then run Maestro in another terminal. Do **not** run Maestro against a stale APK after semantics or presentation edits.

## Authoring and running flows

- Prefer the **Maestro MCP** (`list_devices`, `inspect_screen`, `run`, `cheat_sheet`, `take_screenshot`). Call `cheat_sheet` before authoring unfamiliar commands.
- App id: `app.stackmint.sprout.dev`. Use a development build. Flows use **real OTP sign-in** via `shared/otp-signin-to-overview.yaml` (needs `EMAIL` + `OTP_CODE`). Google account picker is unreliable in Maestro.
- Tap controls by **`Semantics.identifier`** (`tapOn: id: …`), not visible text. IDs are defined in `sprout_app/lib/core/constants/semantics_ids.dart` (`SemanticsIds`). Use `text:` only for dropdown menu items and assertions.
- New tappable UI in presentation must use **`Sprout*` widgets** from `sprout_app/lib/ui/` (exported via `lib/ui/export.dart`) with a `SemanticsIds` value — not raw `FilledButton` / inline `Semantics` wrappers.
- **Root journeys** (`.maestro/*.yaml`) are the only runnable flows; `config.yaml` uses `flows: ["*"]`. **Shared helpers** (`.maestro/shared/*.yaml`) are `runFlow` subflows — no `launchApp`, parameterized via `env`. Reuse helpers instead of duplicating OTP sign-in, seed, or form-fill in a new root journey.
- **Tags**: ordinary PRs use `--include-tags p1` (`full-app-tour`, `otp-auto-submit`, `premium-free-paywalls` — see `.maestro/README.md`). Focused roots use `tags: [page]` (or `auth` / `premium`); smoke (`full-app-tour`, `first-open-online`) use `[smoke]`; no-accounts edges use `[edge]`. Prefer one clearState per shared signed-in setup; keep state-poison edges separate. Filter with `--include-tags`.
- New reusable steps go in `.maestro/shared/` (`seed-core`, `chapter-*`, fill helpers) and are called with `runFlow` + `env`.
- CLI fallback: `maestro test .maestro/` or `maestro test .maestro/<flow>.yaml`.
- Do **not** point ordinary E2E / p1 / smoke Maestro at production. **Exception:** `play-store-screenshots.yaml` (+ `shared/email-otp-human-pause.yaml`, `shared/google-signin-handoff.yaml`, `shared/complete-wizard-play.yaml`) intentionally targets `app.stackmint.sprout` on a **production release** install for banner-free Play listing captures — see `store/play/README.md`. Never reintroduce debug / bypass auth.
